cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'Gyraph: Directed Graph Signal Processing Framework'
message: 'If you use this software, please cite it as below.'
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chan
    given-names: Chun Hei Michael
    email: miki998chan@gmail.com
    affiliation: 'EPFL - MIPLab'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/miki998/GyRAPH'
url: 'https://github.com/miki998/GyRAPH'
abstract: >-
  Gyraph is a comprehensive Python library for directed graph signal
  processing. It extends traditional graph signal processing concepts to
  handle directed graphs, enabling advanced analysis of network flows,
  asymmetric relationships, and directed interactions. The framework includes
  modules for graph construction, operators (Laplacian, advection-diffusion),
  filtering (Wiener, spectral, polynomial), sampling strategies, graph
  learning, signal separation, and surrogate generation.
keywords:
  - graph signal processing
  - directed graphs
  - graph fourier transform
  - graph filtering
  - graph learning
  - signal processing
  - network analysis
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-9'
